shell-lsp: group the fork's own imports apart from other modules

Not for upstream. shell-lsp vendors this module as
github.com/stubbedev/shell-lsp/third_party/mvdan-sh and formats it with
gci, which puts imports from shell-lsp in a section of their own after
the other modules. Once the import paths are rewritten, the two test
files that import another module next to a package of this one need a
blank line between them. In upstream's paths the change is only that
blank line.

diff --git a/expand/expand_test.go b/expand/expand_test.go
index 86f0569..720a0a6 100644
--- a/expand/expand_test.go
+++ b/expand/expand_test.go
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ import (
 	"testing"
 
 	"github.com/go-quicktest/qt"
+
 	"mvdan.cc/sh/v3/syntax"
 )
 
